# Google Drive integration (src/io/googleDrive.js). Copy to `.env.local` and
# fill in to use Drive locally; `.env.local` is not committed.
#
# The values are not passwords: a browser-only app ships them inside its
# bundle, and Google honours them only from the sites they are registered for
# (the OAuth client's JavaScript origins and the API key's website
# restrictions). Development has its own pair, registered for
# http://localhost:5173 only, so the production credentials never accept a
# local origin.
#
# They stay out of the repository so that forks, the Docker image and the
# release zip do not carry identifiers that would fail on their own address.
# The Pages deploy takes the production ones from the repository variables
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_API_KEY and GOOGLE_APP_ID (Settings → Secrets and
# variables → Actions → Variables).
#
# With any of them empty, the Drive entries are left out of the File menu.

# OAuth 2.0 client ID (type "Web application").
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# API key, restricted to the Google Picker API and the app's sites.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# The Cloud project number. The Picker needs it to grant the app access to the
# files picked in it (the drive.file scope only reaches files granted that way).
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
